# Ship-loop terminal states

Ordinary pushed-but-unmerged work is still unfinished. Do not weaken the normal
commit -> push -> PR -> CI -> merge -> live contract and do not treat
`merge-on-green` by itself as completion.

There is one distinct operator-controlled terminal state: **PARKED**.

A pull request is PARKED only when all of these are true:

- its title starts with `HOLD-FOR-SOL`;
- it is still a draft;
- its exact current head is pushed and the worktree is clean;
- it has no `merge-on-green` label and native GitHub auto-merge is not armed;
- the PR body or comments record an explicit Sol authority and a release condition
  controlled by Sol;
- the hold explicitly says not to merge;
- all binding checks on that exact head have concluded clean.

When those conditions hold, the unmerged state is intentional and externally
controlled. Report the work as **PARKED / HOLD-FOR-SOL**, not SHIPPED and not
`SHIP LOOP BLOCKED`. Do not merge, mark ready, arm automation, relabel, or repeatedly
poll/retry merely to satisfy the ordinary merge completion rule. End the session
after one concise evidence report. Resume the ship loop only after Sol releases or
changes the hold.

If any condition above is missing, ambiguous, red, pending, dirty, or stale, fail
closed and follow the ordinary ship loop instead. A vague request to "hold" or
"review later" is never enough to create the PARKED state.

## Pending CI quiescence

A clean exact pushed head with deterministic `ci-plan`, `contract-delta`, and
`fence-pack` green, no binding builder-owned red, and one already-confirmed PR
condition watcher for the same PR/head may enter mechanically derived `CI_QUIESCENT` in the
existing Stop ledger. Logical delivery ownership remains with the session while the
wait consumes **zero new model turns while external state is unchanged**. Repeated
Stop/task notifications do not poll GitHub, narrate, advance the escape ladder, or
create a successor watcher. One green, red, head, hold/authority, or watcher-liveness
change wakes exactly once: green and hold/release changes route to release/Sol;
inherited-main, infrastructure, or missing-evidence events route to
`#6351/main-integrity`; builder-owned red clears the wait and blocks the builder.
The admitted `gh pr checks <PR> --watch --interval 60+` command remains one owner;
the same hook evaluates checks plus hold/review authority as its union condition.
After a material receipt, later Stop boundaries revalidate the event key so an
identical event stays narration-silent but a later same-head red remains visible.
Malformed state fails closed. Only mechanical hook evidence may create quiescence or
PARKED; model prose can never create either state or any terminal truth.
